WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.659 --> 00:00:04.450
It seems like everyone has a theory about
what will happen in the highly anticipated

00:00:04.450 --> 00:00:09.320
Avengers: Infinity War follow-up... and they're
all varying degrees of plausibly implausible.

00:00:09.450 --> 00:00:13.760
But no matter how possible or impossible these
theories seem to be when held up to the light

00:00:13.760 --> 00:00:18.520
of scrutiny, that doesn't stop us from checking
to see if each one is fresh or a real stinker.

00:00:18.580 --> 00:00:23.220
As such, the latest Avengers 4 theory to gain
traction on Reddit where else? has us checking

00:00:23.220 --> 00:00:24.920
our back-issues to see what's what.

00:00:25.240 --> 00:00:29.830
User PhobeterWorse posted a theory that claims
that characters like the Fantastic Four and

00:00:29.830 --> 00:00:34.040
mutants like the characters from the X-Men
franchise have always existed in the Marvel

00:00:34.040 --> 00:00:39.180
Cinematic Universe, but that they'll be introduced
in Avengers 4 following a reversal of Thanos'

00:00:39.180 --> 00:00:41.800
snap that killed half of all living beings.

00:00:44.060 --> 00:00:46.880
The details of the theory are very, very complicated.

00:00:47.260 --> 00:00:49.980
In order to work, it relies on a few different
ideas.

00:00:50.280 --> 00:00:54.550
For the Fantastic Four's introduction, the
theory relies on supergenius Reed Richards

00:00:54.550 --> 00:00:59.170
and the rest of the FF having been off exploring
the Negative Zone, unbeknownst to the rest

00:00:59.170 --> 00:00:59.680
of the world.

00:00:59.920 --> 00:01:04.940
When the snap is undone, they'll be ripped
back into our Earth, at which point an already-established

00:01:04.940 --> 00:01:09.620
Fantastic Four can rejoin the MCU that they've
secretly always been a part of.

00:01:09.840 --> 00:01:13.640
The mutants of the MCU, meanwhile, have an
even more complicated set-up.

00:01:13.860 --> 00:01:18.940
In the theory's telling of the MCU's hidden
history, SHIELD of the 1950s and '60s created

00:01:18.940 --> 00:01:22.920
some kind of bomb to give people superpowers,
but it didn't seem to work.

00:01:23.160 --> 00:01:27.250
Then, as the people hit with the bomb's energy
passed their slightly altered genes to their

00:01:27.250 --> 00:01:32.000
kids, the wave of energy released by the reversed
snap makes the MCU's mutants.

00:01:32.240 --> 00:01:32.740
"NO!

00:01:32.780 --> 00:01:33.780
I'M A MUTANT!"

00:01:33.900 --> 00:01:36.800
Or at least, that's what it all seems to suggest.

00:01:37.000 --> 00:01:40.340
The ins and outs of Reddit theories can be
tough to decipher, and we won't pretend to

00:01:40.340 --> 00:01:42.620
know if we're getting the thing exactly right.

00:01:43.120 --> 00:01:43.620
"What?

00:01:43.840 --> 00:01:44.340
Huh?"

00:01:44.400 --> 00:01:47.020
But there's at least a few kernels of possibility
here.

00:01:47.030 --> 00:01:51.710
For starters, as PhobeterWorse points out,
Marvel Studios president Kevin Feige has hinted

00:01:51.710 --> 00:01:56.620
that future Avengers films will be more space-centric...if
the Avengers survive, that is.

00:01:56.780 --> 00:02:01.220
That gives us a clear path for the Fantastic
Four's arrival from some kind of extra-terrestrial

00:02:01.220 --> 00:02:01.720
setting.

00:02:01.860 --> 00:02:04.820
Then again, this theory is just that: a theory.

00:02:05.000 --> 00:02:08.920
Introducing characters like the X-Men and
the Fantastic Four would definitely change

00:02:08.920 --> 00:02:10.460
the MCU in a major way.

00:02:10.890 --> 00:02:14.780
And fans are driving themselves crazy trying
to figure out how Marvel Studios will work

00:02:14.780 --> 00:02:19.180
them in, now that Marvel's parent company,
Walt Disney Studios, is finally closing in

00:02:19.180 --> 00:02:23.140
on acquiring Fox and all the movie rights
to Marvel characters that it owns.

00:02:23.380 --> 00:02:28.240
It's really only a matter of time until the
X-Men and the Fantastic Four enter the MCU

00:02:28.240 --> 00:02:30.380
and fans definitely expect them to make an
appearance.

00:02:30.660 --> 00:02:34.780
After all, Feige once discussed the importance
of featuring new and different characters

00:02:34.780 --> 00:02:36.060
in Marvel movies in the future:

00:02:36.510 --> 00:02:40.740
"[Evolving Marvel movies is] the most important
thing, and that's what you've seen happen

00:02:40.750 --> 00:02:45.070
over the past 20 films, different genres,
different heroes, heroes maybe you've heard

00:02:45.070 --> 00:02:49.230
of if you'd read comics, heroes you might
not have ever heard of even if you did read

00:02:49.230 --> 00:02:49.720
comics."

00:02:49.840 --> 00:02:55.020
But considering Avengers 4 wrapped principal
photography ages ago since directors Joe and

00:02:55.020 --> 00:03:00.130
Anthony Russo shot Infinity War and Avengers
4 back to back fans probably won't see hide

00:03:00.130 --> 00:03:04.740
nor hair of the X-Men or the Fantastic Four
when the film drops in May 2019.

00:03:04.860 --> 00:03:09.040
Even still, there stands a chance that the
Avengers 4 story could set up the possibility

00:03:09.040 --> 00:03:11.160
of that happening somewhere down the line.

00:03:11.420 --> 00:03:12.880
And it has happened before.

00:03:13.100 --> 00:03:17.380
Don't forget, the aftermath of the first Avengers
film with all the dead aliens and leftover

00:03:17.380 --> 00:03:21.760
tech led to the events that created the Vulture
and his crew in Spider-Man: Homecoming…

00:03:21.980 --> 00:03:26.560
despite writer-director Joss Whedon having
no idea that Sony and Marvel would ever work

00:03:26.560 --> 00:03:29.160
out their differences to bring Spidey into
the MCU.

00:03:29.300 --> 00:03:31.880
It worked then, so it can probably work now.

00:03:36.420 --> 00:03:39.920
So how will the Fantastic Four, the X-Men,
and the rest of Marvel's mutants make their

00:03:39.930 --> 00:03:40.940
way to the MCU?

00:03:40.940 --> 00:03:45.290
Well, we've got a big purple dude who can
snap his hot dog fingers and change the very

00:03:45.290 --> 00:03:47.040
fabric of reality in an instant.

00:03:47.440 --> 00:03:51.160
So it doesn't really need to any more complicated
than that...if you think about it with your

00:03:51.160 --> 00:03:51.660
brain, that is.

00:03:51.920 --> 00:03:59.340
"The brain is a muscle and this is a muscle
and they are all muscles so I'm covered in

00:03:59.350 --> 00:04:01.120
brains so I've got more brains than you."

